load @term/seed/code/group
  find group

# The orthogonal group: the group of linear maps that preserve length, the rotations and reflections of a space with a
# fixed inner product. In n dimensions it is O(n). It splits into the rotations (determinant one) and the
# length-preserving reflections (determinant minus one). The orthogonal group of the eight-dimensional arena, O(8), is
# where the rotations giving D4 live. The form carries the underlying group; preserving the inner product is the
# defining condition.
form orthogonal-group
  link group, like group
